Google Apps Script runs inside Google Workspace — it's JavaScript that lives inside your Google Sheets, Docs, and Forms and triggers automatically. No server needed. Free forever.

### **Setting Up Google Apps Script**

Every Google Sheet has its own built-in script editor:

**Step 1:** Open any Google Sheet

**Step 2:** Click "Extensions" → "Apps Script"

**Step 3:** The Apps Script editor opens in a new tab. This is where you paste and run scripts.

**Step 4:** Paste your script → click "Save" → click "Run" (first run will ask for permissions — click through and grant them)

**Step 5:** For scripts that should run automatically: click "Triggers" (the clock icon in the left sidebar) → "Add Trigger" → set the function and schedule

---

### **Apps Script 1: Lead Tracking Dashboard**

This script reads your subscriber tracking sheet and generates a summary tab with:

* Total subscribers to date  
* New subscribers this week vs last week (percentage change)  
* Day of week with most opt-ins  
* Average daily opt-ins over the last 30 days

**Paste this into your Apps Script editor:**

function updateDashboard() {

  const ss \= SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();

  const dataSheet \= ss.getSheetByName('Subscribers');

  const dashSheet \= ss.getSheetByName('Dashboard') || ss.insertSheet('Dashboard');

  const data \= dataSheet.getDataRange().getValues();

  const headers \= data\[0\];

  const rows \= data.slice(1);

  const dateCol \= headers.indexOf('Date');

  const emailCol \= headers.indexOf('Email');

  const today \= new Date();

  const oneWeekAgo \= new Date(today.getTime() \- 7 \* 24 \* 60 \* 60 \* 1000);

  const twoWeeksAgo \= new Date(today.getTime() \- 14 \* 24 \* 60 \* 60 \* 1000);

  let thisWeek \= 0;

  let lastWeek \= 0;

  let last30Days \= 0;

  const dayCount \= \[0,0,0,0,0,0,0\];

  rows.forEach(row \=\> {

    if (\!row\[dateCol\]) return;

    const rowDate \= new Date(row\[dateCol\]);



    if (rowDate \>= oneWeekAgo) thisWeek++;

    if (rowDate \>= twoWeeksAgo && rowDate \< oneWeekAgo) lastWeek++;

    if (rowDate \>= new Date(today.getTime() \- 30 \* 24 \* 60 \* 60 \* 1000)) last30Days++;

    dayCount\[rowDate.getDay()\]++;

  });

  const days \= \['Sunday','Monday','Tuesday','Wednesday','Thursday','Friday','Saturday'\];

  const bestDay \= days\[dayCount.indexOf(Math.max(...dayCount))\];

  const weekChange \= lastWeek \> 0 ? (((thisWeek \- lastWeek) / lastWeek) \* 100).toFixed(1) : 'N/A';

  const avgDaily \= (last30Days / 30).toFixed(1);

  dashSheet.clearContents();

  dashSheet.getRange('A1').setValue('SUBSCRIBER DASHBOARD').setFontWeight('bold').setFontSize(14);

  dashSheet.getRange('A2').setValue('Last updated: ' \+ today.toLocaleString());

  dashSheet.getRange('A4:B4').setValues(\[\['Total Subscribers', rows.filter(r \=\> r\[emailCol\]).length\]\]);

  dashSheet.getRange('A5:B5').setValues(\[\['This Week', thisWeek\]\]);

  dashSheet.getRange('A6:B6').setValues(\[\['Last Week', lastWeek\]\]);

  dashSheet.getRange('A7:B7').setValues(\[\['Week-over-Week Change', weekChange \+ '%'\]\]);

  dashSheet.getRange('A8:B8').setValues(\[\['Avg Daily (30 days)', avgDaily\]\]);

  dashSheet.getRange('A9:B9').setValues(\[\['Best Day of Week', bestDay\]\]);

  SpreadsheetApp.flush();

  Logger.log('Dashboard updated.');

}

**Set it to run automatically:**

* Apps Script → Triggers → Add Trigger  
* Function: `updateDashboard`  
* Event source: Time-driven  
* Type: Day timer  
* Time: 6am–7am (runs every morning before you wake up)

