### **Apps Script 3: Bill Tracker \+ Telegram Reminder**

This one is a quality-of-life automation that also applies to your business expenses. It monitors a "Bills Due" sheet and sends you a Telegram message 3 days before any bill is due.

**Sheet structure:** `Bill Name | Amount | Due Date | Paid? | Notes`

function checkUpcomingBills() {

  const sheet \= SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet().getSheetByName('Bills');

  const data \= sheet.getDataRange().getValues();

  const today \= new Date();

  const threeDays \= new Date(today.getTime() \+ 3 \* 24 \* 60 \* 60 \* 1000);

  const upcoming \= \[\];

  data.slice(1).forEach((row, i) \=\> {

    const billName \= row\[0\];

    const amount \= row\[1\];

    const dueDate \= new Date(row\[2\]);

    const paid \= row\[3\];



    if (\!billName || paid \=== 'YES' || paid \=== true) return;



    if (dueDate \<= threeDays && dueDate \>= today) {

      upcoming.push(\`• ${billName}: $${amount} due ${dueDate.toLocaleDateString()}\`);

    }

  });

  if (upcoming.length \=== 0\) return;

  const message \= \`⚠️ Bills Due Soon:\\n\\n${upcoming.join('\\n')}\`;

  const telegramToken \= 'YOUR\_BOT\_TOKEN';

  const chatId \= 'YOUR\_CHAT\_ID';

  const url \= \`https://api.telegram.org/bot${telegramToken}/sendMessage\`;

  UrlFetchApp.fetch(url, {

    method: 'post',

    contentType: 'application/json',

    payload: JSON.stringify({ chat\_id: chatId, text: message })

  });

}

**Trigger:** Run daily at 8am.

Replace `YOUR_BOT_TOKEN` with your Telegram bot token and `YOUR_CHAT_ID` with your chat ID.

