Cloudflare Workers are small pieces of JavaScript that run on Cloudflare's global network. They're perfect for things that need to be on the internet 24/7 and respond instantly — like a webhook receiver, an API endpoint, or a scheduled background job.

You already have a Cloudflare account. Workers are free up to 100,000 requests per day.

### **Use Case 1: Deal Site Auto-Updater**

If you built a deal site in Module 2, this Worker runs on a schedule (Cloudflare Cron Trigger) and updates your deals from an Amazon feed automatically.

We'll go deep on building the full deal site Worker in the supplementary deal site build guide — but here's the shape of what it does:

export default {

  async scheduled(event, env, ctx) {

    // Fetch fresh deals from your deals source

    const deals \= await fetchDeals(env);



    // Store updated deals in Cloudflare KV

    await env.DEALS\_KV.put('latest\_deals', JSON.stringify(deals));



    // Send Telegram notification

    await notifyTelegram(env.TELEGRAM\_TOKEN, env.CHAT\_ID, 

      \`Deal site updated: ${deals.length} deals refreshed.\`);

  }

}

### **Use Case 2: Webhook Receiver for Form Submissions**

Instead of relying on Zapier or a third-party service to catch your form submissions, a Cloudflare Worker can receive the webhook, process it, and fan it out to multiple destinations simultaneously.

export default {

  async fetch(request, env) {

    if (request.method \!== 'POST') {

      return new Response('Method not allowed', { status: 405 });

    }



    const data \= await request.json();

    const { email, name, source } \= data;



    // Add to MailerLite

    await addToMailerLite(email, name, env.MAILERLITE\_API\_KEY);



    // Log to Google Sheets (via Google Apps Script web app)

    await logToSheets(email, name, source, env.SHEETS\_WEBHOOK\_URL);



    // Send Telegram notification

    await sendTelegram(env.TELEGRAM\_TOKEN, env.CHAT\_ID,

      \`New lead: ${name} (${email}) from ${source}\`);



    return new Response(JSON.stringify({ success: true }), {

      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' }

    });

  }

}

We'll deploy Workers properly in the Module 2 supplementary guide. For now, know that they exist, they're free, and they're how your deal site runs without any server cost.

